{
  "name": "l0_target_name_predicates",
  "about": "`CBaseEntity::HasTarget` 0x100a1b40 (slot 160) and `CBaseEntity::HasLinkedDoor` 0x100a1c30 (slot 161) are the same 177 bytes under two trace labels (`walks/L0-r020.md`): after the scope-trace push, `name == NULL` -> 0 (`100a1baa`), `m_target` (+0x20c) `== NULL` -> 0 (`100a1bb2`), else `__strcmpi(name, m_target) == 0` (`100a1bc5`, the CRT C-locale ASCII fold: case-blind, byte-exact otherwise). `m_iName` (+0x26c) is read for the trace label only and never decides the answer; nothing is written. An authored `target` that is blank is stored as NULL by the datadesc string parse `AllocPooledString` 0x1042bff0, so NULL and empty are one case. Their one dispatch site each passes the CALLER's own targetname: `FUN_101331e0` asks every `multi_manager` `HasTarget(this->m_iName)`; `FUN_100efbf0` (the SDK `UpdateAreaPortals`) asks every `func_areaportal` `HasLinkedDoor(door->m_iName)` and then `Use(door, door, open ? USE_ON : USE_OFF, 0)`. Three `logic_relay`s created at runtime stand for the asked entity: `Other` (target `Door_A`), `Door_A` (target `Door_A`, its own name) and `NoTarget` (no `target` key). The seven retail rows: Door_A/Other asked `Door_A` -> 1; Door_A/Door_A asked `door_a` -> 1 (the fold), `Door_B` -> 0, `Door_A ` (trailing space) -> 0, NULL -> 0; NoTarget asked `Door_A` -> 0 and NULL -> 0. Each row runs on both slots. Reported as `fail`, a result or a site payload differs from retail's.",
  "stage": "arena",
  "seed": 1,
  "duration": 1.2,
